  "body": "### Summary\nAs the orchestrator, I want one parser for the `Closes #N` / `Refs #N` line of a PR, so that a body the Issue and claim check accepts is also one the sweep closes and the ledger folds. Today a PR can pass the check and be invisible to the sweep, with no report.\n\n### Scenario (probed in Python against the three modules)\n- `LOT-012 · Closes #45`, `- Closes #77`, `**Closes #12**` and `Closed #9` pass the claim check (`linked_issues` returns the number); `hygiene.CLOSES` finds nothing, so the sweep's `close` action never closes the issue after the merge.\n- For the first two bodies, and for `Fixes #123`, `ledger.issue_number` falls back to the PR number: a correct `gap-new` row `GAP-<issue>` is then refused (`tooling/docs/ledger.py:140-141`).\n- `Refs #893 for the device check.` followed by `Closes #50`: the ledger takes 893 as the PR's issue, so the new row must be `GAP-893`; the claim check also requires #893 open and claimed by the same id (`scripts/issue_claims.py:128-143`).\n\n### Evidence (`7a61018f`)\n- `scripts/issue_claims.py:30`: `\\b(?:close[sd]?|fix(?:e[sd])?|resolve[sd]?|refs?)\\s+#(\\d+)\\b`, anywhere in the body.\n- `tooling/roadmap/hygiene.py:82-83`: `^[ \\t]*(?:closes|fixes|resolves)[ \\t]+#(\\d+)\\b`, line start only.\n- `tooling/docs/ledger.py:50`: `^[ \\t]*(?:closes|refs)[ \\t]+#(\\d+)\\b` (no `fixes`), and `:90-93` `issue_number` takes the first match, a `Refs` included.\n- Each script's tests use its own regex; `scripts/tests/ledger_real_bodies.json` holds three bodies, all canonical.\n\n### Fix\nOne shared parser (e.g. `tooling/common/pr_refs.py`: closing refs, `Refs`, the primary issue = the first closing ref, never a `Refs` when a `Closes` exists), imported by the three scripts. One grammar: the check rejects what the sweep cannot read, or the sweep reads what the check accepts.\n\n### Test (fails today on five bodies)\n`test_pr_refs_agree`: a table of bodies (the six above plus `Closes #50, #51`) giving the same closing set from `issue_claims.linked_issues`, `hygiene.CLOSES` and `ledger.issue_number`.\n\nHow many merged PR bodies use a variant was not counted. Rework model: Sonnet 5.5, reviewed by Opus 5.5.\n\nFound by #775 (cloud/r775-fable, Fable 5.2). Reviewed at `dev-swift` @ `7a61018f`; read from the code, not run on a device unless stated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
